+				Vec3 vNormal = RoadSurfaceNormal(bFollowIntegrated, vWSPos, 0.25f * fStep / unitSize);
 
 				Vec3 vBiTang = pVerts[1] - pVerts[0];
 				vBiTang.Normalize();
@@ -618,10 +752,18 @@ void CRoadRenderNode::OnTerrainChanged()
 
 	Vec3 vWSBoxCenter = m_serializedData.worldSpaceBBox.GetCenter(); //vWSBoxCenter.z=0;
 
+	// This is only the interim refresh; ScheduleRebuild(true) below has Compile() redo the mesh from
+	// Update(). It still has to read the same surface the full rebuild will, otherwise the road snaps
+	// back onto the bare heightmap for a frame wherever an object is rendering as terrain.
+	const bool bFollowIntegrated = (GetCVars()->e_RoadsFollowIntegratedObjects != 0);
+	SIntegratedHeightScope heightScope(bFollowIntegrated, m_serializedData.worldSpaceBBox);
+
 	for (int i = 0, nVertsNum = m_pRenderMesh->GetVerticesCount(); i < nVertsNum; i++)
 	{
 		Vec3& vPos = *(Vec3*)&pPos[i * nPosStride];
-		vPos.z = GetTerrain()->GetZApr(vWSBoxCenter.x + vPos.x, vWSBoxCenter.y + vPos.y) + 0.01f - vWSBoxCenter.z;
+		const float fX = vWSBoxCenter.x + vPos.x;
+		const float fY = vWSBoxCenter.y + vPos.y;
+		vPos.z = RoadSurfaceZ(bFollowIntegrated, fX, fY, GetTerrain()->GetZApr(fX, fY)) + 0.01f - vWSBoxCenter.z;
 	}
 	m_pRenderMesh->UnlockStream(VSF_GENERAL);
 
diff --git a/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp b/Code/CryEngine/Cry3DEngine/cvars.cpp
